.TH AVR\-GROUP\-MEMBER\-ADD 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-group-member-add \- Add members to a group.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr group member add
[OPTIONS] GROUP [MEMBER]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add members to a group.
.PP
GROUP is a group ID (grp-...), the group's path from the root group, such as Organization/Platform/CI, or the end of a path when only one group has it, such as Platform/CI.
.PP
Name each MEMBER by user ID (usr-...), @me or a verified email address, as arguments or one per line with --file, where a line starting with # is a comment unless it is an email address, such as #ops@example.com. The command adds them all in one change, up to 250, and reports each member's result; a member already in the state asked for counts as done, so a rerun is safe.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr group member add Platform/CI @me
    avr group member add Platform/CI usr-0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef
    avr group member add Platform/CI --file members.txt
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    action, detail, member, status, user_id
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIGROUP\fR
\&
.TP
[\fIMEMBER...\fR]
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR \fITEXT\fR
Read members from a file, one per line; - reads standard input.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-group-member (1),
.BR avr-group-member-list (1),
.BR avr-group-member-remove (1)
